<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank market closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank market closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended firmer outperforming other European counterpart after the final approval of the 1997 budget law.</p>
<p>The 10-year spread over Bunds declined to 111 basis points from 118 bps at the yesterday's close, while the long term future contract hit a high at 112.25.</p>
<p>But a dull trade, due to the holiday season, limited the gains. The tone of the &quot;could improve a little on Monday, but I really do not expect nothing serious before the next year,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
